  "area": "stitches",
  "title": "Six scattered fill squares in three colours, saved before and after Optimize Sewing Order",
  "description": "Six 15 mm fill squares at (10,10) red, (70,70) blue, (70,10) red, (10,70) green, (40,40) blue, (40,10) green, imported from an SVG in that order. PE-DESIGN 11.50 groups them into three colour blocks in first-occurrence order (red, blue, green), visiting red top-left, red top-right, blue bottom-right, blue centre, green bottom-left, green top-centre. The Sewing Order pane's Optimize Sewing Order button changed nothing on this design (the two files differ in 4 header bytes only). Issue #137: OpenStitch's order.optimize is compared with the colour blocks and stitch counts of both files.",
